hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"19166","Abd Allah ibn Muhammad narrated to us. Abd Allah said: And I heard it from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Shayba. Marwan ibn Muawiya al-Fazari narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Taifi, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Khalid al-Adwani, from his father, that he saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the east of Thaqif while he stood upon a bow or a staff when he came to them seeking support. He said: So I heard him recite: By the sky and the night-comer, until he completed it. He said: So I memorized it in ignorance while a polytheist, then I recited it in Islam. He said: So Thaqif called me and said: What did you hear from this man? So I recited it to them. So those with them of Quraysh said: We know our companion best; had we known what he says is true we would have followed him."
